			<div class="content" id="post-content-1948323">
									

<p>A minor nitpick here (seriously, minor, but it bugged me):</p>
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-1741-C is a male humanoid of European descent, dressed in zoot suit.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>And</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Background study has revealed that Alan Pearce went missing in 1946.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Okay, so Alan Pearce (who 1741-C resembles) disappeared in 1946. While a <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zoot_suit">zoot suit</a> is from that era, it's unlikely he'd be wearing one. They were usually worn by younger men for nightclubbing, and were usually seen as extravagant and flashy - especially during the wartime, when there was fabric rationing.</p>
<p>So maybe it could be a plain men's suit in a dark grey? Or a trouser/sweater vest/shirt combination? Or, since it could be said he's a bit of a carny, plain brown trousers and a rumpled white shirt with folded up shirtsleeves.</p>

